[statement]
A package installed for its `install_if` condition ends the chain of
requirements: `base` and `top` are requested, `q` is installed for its
condition on `base` and needs `n`, `top` needs `z`, and `z` needs `q`.
`n` 2 needs `missing`, and `n` 1 needs `z`; apk chooses `n` 2 and
refuses, since no requirement brought `q`. Where `q` has no condition and
`z` alone requires it, `z` is up the chain, and apk passes `n` 2 over, as
`a-candidate-whose-dependency-cannot-be-met-is-passed-over-beside-one-depending-further-up`.

[repository]
P:base
V:1

P:q
V:1
i:base
D:n

P:top
V:1
D:z

P:z
V:1
D:q

P:n
V:2
D:missing

P:n
V:1
D:z

[request]
base
top

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
